1
00:00:56,581 --> 00:00:59,559
There is a way, Malcolm.

2
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:04,367
We get our friends to roll their sleeves up and get to work.

3
00:01:04,367 --> 00:01:05,515
It's certainly a good idea.

4
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:08,493
If I could take a look at the place,

5
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:11,471
I could probably tell what it requires to fix it up.

6
00:01:11,471 --> 00:01:15,065
How much paint, how many hours of work ...

7
00:01:15,065 --> 00:01:18,976
That's what I came to ask you to do, Malcolm.

8
00:01:18,976 --> 00:01:21,005
If you would supervise the refurbishing,

9
00:01:21,005 --> 00:01:25,863
I'll find the people to help do it.

10
00:01:25,863 --> 00:01:26,685
I'll help too, Mr. Baker.

11
00:01:26,685 --> 00:01:30,386
I can get some of my friends to go around the neighborhood

12
00:01:30,386 --> 00:01:31,957
and collect the furniture we need.

13
00:01:31,957 --> 00:01:33,317
I'll help.

14
00:01:33,317 --> 00:01:38,273
Tomorrow. Yes. We'll meet tomorrow morning, right here.

15
00:01:38,273 --> 00:01:40,073
Can we help?

16
00:01:40,073 --> 00:01:42,473
I'd really like to.

17
00:01:42,473 --> 00:01:42,673
Sure.

18
00:01:42,473 --> 00:01:44,229
We might need you to come through with your friends, Robbie.

19
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:47,029
Not just to go around the neighborhood asking for furniture,

20
00:01:47,029 --> 00:01:49,487
but to help with the paint job.

21
00:01:49,487 --> 00:01:52,810
That's backbreaking work and may be too much for us.

22
00:01:52,810 --> 00:01:55,734
I'll do it. I'll talk to them.

23
00:01:55,734 --> 00:01:59,118
And tomorrow morning we'll all meet here to discuss the plan?

24
00:01:59,118 --> 00:02:19,964
Tomorrow morning it is.

25
00:02:19,964 --> 00:02:31,876
Come in, come in. Please, come in.

26
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:36,140
I'd like you to meet my friend Malcolm Stewart.

27
00:02:36,140 --> 00:02:38,683
Malcolm, this is Joanne Thompson. Malcolm

28
00:02:38,683 --> 00:02:41,185
Hello, Joanne. Nice to meet you.

29
00:02:41,185 --> 00:02:42,310
My pleasure, Malcolm.

30
00:02:42,310 --> 00:02:45,455
And this is Abe Lucas. You must remember Abe.

31
00:02:45,455 --> 00:02:49,266
He ran the drugstore

32
00:02:49,266 --> 00:02:49,744
and used to play drums with the jazz band on weekends.

33
00:02:49,744 --> 00:02:51,472
Oh, sure I do. Hi, Abe.

34
00:02:51,472 --> 00:02:52,722
Hello, Mr. Stewart.

35
00:02:52,722 --> 00:02:54,082
Malcolm, please.

36
00:02:54,082 --> 00:02:55,700
Hello, Malcolm.

37
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:57,800
Sit down, sit down. Have some coffee.

38
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:01,656
And I've got some delicious Danish pastry for you.

39
00:03:01,656 --> 00:03:04,634
Where's your grandson Robbie and his friend Alexandra?

40
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:07,612
Weren't they going to be here this morning?

41
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:10,589
I thought so, too.

42
00:03:10,589 --> 00:03:12,989
I'm surprised they're not here.

43
00:03:12,989 --> 00:03:16,545
Robbie left early this morning to meet Alexandra. Robbie

44
00:03:16,545 --> 00:03:20,523
Frankly, I thought they'd be here, but ...

45
00:03:20,523 --> 00:03:23,358
It's OK. I'm sure they meant well,

46
00:03:23,358 --> 00:03:25,287
but they probably had other things on their minds.

47
00:03:25,287 --> 00:03:28,457
I understand you used to be in the construction business,

48
00:03:28,457 --> 00:03:30,281
Malcolm. Malcolm。

49
00:03:30,281 --> 00:03:31,435
I was, indeed.

50
00:03:31,435 --> 00:03:34,413
I wonder if you would take a look at the old library

51
00:03:34,413 --> 00:03:37,391
and make sure that it is in good condition

52
00:03:37,391 --> 00:03:40,369
so that we don't have to worry about any structural problems.

53
00:03:40,369 --> 00:03:44,339
When can I do that? I'd be happy to.

54
00:03:44,339 --> 00:03:46,818
We've got permission to go inside the old building

55
00:03:46,818 --> 00:03:48,792
during the week--

56
00:03:48,792 --> 00:03:50,663
Tuesday or Wednesday.

57
00:03:50,663 --> 00:03:52,281
That's fine with me. I can do it either day.

58
00:03:52,281 --> 00:03:55,259
That would be very helpful.

59
00:03:55,259 --> 00:03:58,237
I think the building just needs a good cleaning.

60
00:03:58,237 --> 00:04:01,515
And a good paint job.

61
00:04:01,515 --> 00:04:03,315
Then we have to furnish it.

62
00:04:03,315 --> 00:04:06,193
I wish Robbie and Alexandra had come to this meeting.

63
00:04:06,193 --> 00:04:11,441
They had some ideas about getting the place fixed up.

64
00:04:11,441 --> 00:04:13,127
Perhaps they'll show up. In the meantime,

65
00:04:13,127 --> 00:04:18,105
let me give you some additional thoughts and ideas I have.

66
00:04:18,105 --> 00:04:19,083
OK.

67
00:04:19,083 --> 00:04:21,003
Go ahead, Joanne.

68
00:04:21,003 --> 00:04:25,038
As I said, mostly the building just needs a good cleaning.

69
00:04:25,038 --> 00:04:28,016
This place can be developed

70
00:04:28,016 --> 00:04:32,354
with one real intergenerational program.

71
00:04:32,354 --> 00:04:33,972
That's an idea I like.

72
00:04:33,972 --> 00:04:35,097
A community center

73
00:04:35,097 --> 00:04:38,236
with the kinds of programs that fit everyone.

74
00:04:38,236 --> 00:04:41,608
And programs that don't leave anyone out.

75
00:04:41,608 --> 00:04:43,237
It's asking a lot.

76
00:04:43,237 --> 00:04:46,784
But we can't do it without talking to the young people.

77
00:04:46,784 --> 00:04:48,862
Finding out what they want.

78
00:04:48,862 --> 00:04:51,342
If only Robbie and Alexandra were here.

79
00:04:51,342 --> 00:04:52,658
Don't be upset, Malcolm.

80
00:04:52,658 --> 00:04:55,626
We'll have a chance to talk to them later.

81
00:04:55,626 --> 00:04:57,796
It's not like Robbie.

82
00:04:57,796 --> 00:05:00,774
If he says he's going to be here, he's here.

83
00:05:00,774 --> 00:05:03,774
I wonder what the problem is.
